2
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.439
{\an8}He's late.

3
00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:20.999
{\an8}Christ. you'd think
the bloody Pope's coming round.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.839
{\an8}You put the champagne
in the fridge?

5
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.119
{\an8}No.

6
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.000
{\an8}Just stick it in the freezer.

7
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.680
{\an8}- He's here!
- Oh. finally.

8
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.560
{\an8}- Come on. he's here!
- Okay.

9
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.720
{\an8}- Thanks. mate.
- All right. mate. No worries.

10
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.560
- Hiya. Mum.
- Oh. Tommy. come here.

11
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.559
Oh!

12
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.840
- Hiya. mate.
- Hiya. mate.

13
00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.320
Hiya. Dad.

14
00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.719
Three months in the Falklands.

15
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.639
counting sheep and looking for Argie boats
that never bloody came.

16
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:09.119
Then Brunei. ten weeks with the Gurkhas.

17
00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.959
marching through the jungle
in 90% humidity.

18
00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.919
It was like wearing your kit
in a fuckin' sauna.

19
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.639
Oi. you're home now. None of that.

20
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.959
Then it was Germany
for the live-fire exercises.

21
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:22.599
- And Cyprus for R and R.
- That means gettin' pissed.

22
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.359
- No. it doesn't.
- It means getting pissed. Mum.

23
00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.400
- It's Richie.
- Oh. nice one.

24
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.559
- He's just back.
- He can see his pals.

25
00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.279
Richie's all right.

26
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.999
Auntie Beryl's round tomorrow.
He can't be full of drink.

27
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.920
- That's the only way to deal with Beryl.
- Uh. watch it.

28
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.039
- I'm goin' for a pint.
- You've not finished!

29
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.439
Mum. I 'ave now.

30
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.519
Hey. be careful. will you?

31
00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:50.560
There's all these stories round the city.
That poor kid that died.

32
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.200
I can strip a machine gun
blindfolded. Mum.

33
00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.440
This is Liverpool.

34
00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.560
I think I can handle it.

35
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:00.279
Oh. go on.

36
00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.799
Sorry. the room's spinnin'.

37
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.360
- You need to come down.
- Have you got any weed?

38
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.239
I can do better than that.

39
00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.400
Sure?

40
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.360
Yeah. go on. then.

41
00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.120
- Hiya.
- You all right?

42
00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.600
- Hi.
- Hi.

43
00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:45.920
Have you got any more?

44
00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.720
You got money?

45
00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.320
Yeah.

46
00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:58.839
Do it yourself.

47
00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.719
Oi! You're not gonna get far
without that.

48
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.759
Thanks. Mum.
I'll try and get longer next time.

49
00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.479
- Yeah. and write some bloody letters too.
- I will.

50
00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:21.600
- Love you. Mum.
- I love you.

51
00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.919
- Bye. mate.
- Bye. mate.

52
00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.759
Bye. Dad.

53
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.000
Bye. son.

54
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:08.280
Train station. yeah?

55
00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.080
No.

56
00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.639
So you're in the field.
spending money hand over fist.

57
00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.239
and so far. the main development

58
00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.359
is Liverpool and the Turks
realizing that they should work together.

59
00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.519
That's good. If they work together.
it means we can take them down together.

60
00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:34.039
And how might you do that?

61
00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.239
The Turks will source it.
Liverpool will distribute.

62
00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:39.359
What they're missing is an importer
who can handle the increased load.

63
00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.959
I need to make that my job.

64
00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.039
Then I've got eyes
on the whole Turkish operation.

65
00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.360
and we can dismantle it
and nick the lot of them.

66
00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:49.719
And if we can work out
the Liverpool distribution network.

67
00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.639
then we can take 'em down
at the same time.

68
00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:54.959
Achieve all that. and we pull off
the biggest result in Customs history.

69
00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.279
And if not.
we've played a not insignificant part

70
00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:00.879
in creating the most powerful drugs cartel
this country has ever seen.

71
00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:03.199
Yeah. well. there is that.

72
00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.960
I've heard quite enough
of these future glories. Don.

73
00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.519
Next time you call me.
call me with progress.

74
00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:09.600
Absolutely. sir.

75
00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.879
He'll pull it. by the way.

76
00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.759
If he thinks it's coming apart.
he'll pull it himself.

77
00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.920
So let's find him some progress.

78
00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:30.959
Who should we be looking out for
amongst the Turks?

79
00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.360
- No one. You worry about Liverpool.
- You don't tell me what to do. mate.

80
00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.599
Look. Guy's right.

81
00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.479
The targets have come together.
but we keep the operations apart.

82
00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:43.119
That way. if one of the operations
gets busted. the other one survives.

83
00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.639
Shouldn't we pool our intelligence?

84
00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:48.159
When undercover. the only thing worse than
knowing too little is knowing too much.

85
00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.119
If you react to a face or a name that your
legend shouldn't know. it's game over.

86
00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:54.159
You lot tell me what I need to know.

87
00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.799
and I'll tell the other operation
what they need to know.

88
00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:58.360
So. we're done.

89
00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.119
What's wrong with him?
I mean. he was never exactly chatty. but…

90
00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.440
He's in legend.

91
00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.799
And the kind of legend he's building
is the kind you're never really out of.

92
00:08:18.840 --> 00:08:21.119
How do you get it in?

93
00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.480
How do you distribute it?

94
00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.080
Hmm.

95
00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.400
All you need to know
is we bring it in pure.

96
00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.679
All we need to know
is you can help build the network.

97
00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.480
We control half of Britain.

98
00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.559
If this stuff's as good as you say it is.
then we'll control the other half too.

99
00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:39.040
Okay. okay.

100
00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:41.080
We do a test run.

101
00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.240
Then we'll see you at the dogs.

102
00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.800
Battery. transmitter.

103
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.600
Uh. fixings.

104
00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:54.040
Okay.

105
00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:56.360
No idea what that is.

106
00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.959
- Good luck.
- Aren't you gonna show me how to make it?

107
00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.439
Show you? It's not <i>Blue Peter.</i>

108
00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:04.080
Figure it out for yourself.

109
00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:07.640
- Show you!
- Go on then. what you got?

110
00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.079
Eddie McKee. long record.
firearms and violence.

111
00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.439
- Though nothing for a while.
- Mmm.

112
00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:17.840
Then there's… Declan Carter.

113
00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:19.680
The good-looking one.

114
00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.839
That's inappropriate. Anything?

115
00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:27.319
No. nothing. No record of any nature.
which I found unlikely.

116
00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:31.200
so I went through Liverpool court records.

117
00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:33.080
and there they were.

118
00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:35.199
Historical charges.

119
00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:37.759
Loan sharking. money with menaces.
that kind of thing.

120
00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.039
So the charges were dropped?

121
00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:43.719
Before the case came to court.
every time. which is… It's interesting.

122
00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.919
- You got an address?
- Mmm. no. I'll get one.

123
00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.000
It's proving harder
than it should be. but…

124
00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:50.279
Well. that's interesting too.

125
00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:51.880
Yeah. It is.

126
00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:55.559
Birmingham.

127
00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:56.639
You what?

128
00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.479
We have a package for you
in Istanbul.

129
00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:00.599
You must show that
you can ship it to Felixstowe.

130
00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.999
get it past customs
and take it to a handover in Birmingham.

131
00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:06.719
- Why not a handover in Liverpool?
- Because we don't trust them.

132
00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.720
And they don't trust us yet.
So we meet halfway.

133
00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:11.560
Where's the handover?

134
00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:13.519
A dog track in Birmingham.

135
00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.239
It's too public.

136
00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:20.759
Of course public. Nobody dies in public.

137
00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.679
- It's only a test run.
- Oh. okay.

138
00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:24.839
I'll tell the judge
it was only a test run.

139
00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.799
This is what is happening.
and now you know what is happening.

140
00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:30.560
so if you're not going to do it.
then I have a problem.

141
00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.440
Do you want me to have a problem?

142
00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:43.799
I'll do it. but next time. I'll be in the
meetin' you had before this meetin'. okay?

143
00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:47.360
Don't worry about other meetings.
If this does not work.

144
00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.840
there will not be other meetings.

145
00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.839
- We gotta let it through.
- Let what through?

146
00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:59.599
- Whatever comes in at Felixstowe.
- Are you taking the piss?

147
00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:00.719
It's a test. a small load.

148
00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.239
And if it works. he'll do a big load.
and when I say a big load.

149
00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:05.559
I reckon we're lookin'
at the biggest heroin importation

150
00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.079
this country's ever seen.

151
00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.479
That's what we're working towards.
and we need to make sure we get there.

152
00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.479
So we let this one through
and we pick it up somewhere down the line.

153
00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:17.760
That's called importing drugs.
It's sort of the opposite of what we do.

154
00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.359
You can get it on a boat into Felixstowe

155
00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.279
by promising
that it stays under Customs control.

156
00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.719
but it couldn't go near the public.

157
00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:26.680
They're watching me like a hawk.

158
00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.679
We can't knock over this job

159
00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:32.239
without me looking like Customs.
Old Bill. or useless.

160
00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:35.440
- Which of those options end well for me?
- This is your job. son.

161
00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.879
To get into situations like this
and find ways out of them.

162
00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.160
So let me know when you've got a plan.

163
00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.960
So. how'd you end up in Customs. then?

164
00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.400
I was a clever kid.

165
00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.400
Bit full of meself too.
if you can believe that.

166
00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:06.920
Yeah. I can believe that.

167
00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:11.279
I wanted to go to university.

168
00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.000
but when I went up there
for the interview. I couldn't go in.

169
00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.440
I knew I didn't belong in that world.
and I couldn't get past it.

170
00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.199
But it was all right.
Me dad said. "Don't worry."

171
00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:25.240
"You don't have to go there
to do somethin' special with your life."

172
00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:29.519
He said if I joined Customs.
I'd see the world.

173
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.559
I reckon he was probably thinkin'
of the Navy.

174
00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.239
seeing as I ended up
chasing perverts around Essex.

175
00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.159
Now here I am.

176
00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:41.679
Back in a world I don't belong in.
But this time. I ain't going home.

177
00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:44.240
Well. I'm glad one of us
doesn't feel out of their depth.

178
00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:47.320
Course I do.

179
00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:54.600
This is bloody dangerous.
and we're just civil servants. Bailey.

180
00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:59.999
But I reckon that knowing that
and knowing how hard we have to work at it

181
00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.320
might just give us half a chance
of getting through it.

182
00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.079
Let's hope you're right.

183
00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:10.360
That sounded good. Did that sound good?

184
00:13:18.960 --> 00:13:24.400
That's everyone out that went in.
All the couriers and all of Carter's men.

185
00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.520
You sure?

186
00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:30.039
No. You sure that's gonna work?

187
00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.040
Nah.

188
00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:37.240
Well. then. I suppose we better find out
just how out of our depth we really are.

189
00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.120
We're here.

190
00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:20.520
Take that.

191
00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:28.320
Come on.

192
00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:39.520
Done.

193
00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.080
I think.

194
00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:44.760
Let's go.

195
00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:01.599
Fuck. It's a different code to get out.

196
00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.680
Shit.

197
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:12.839
- If he knew. he would've told us.
- I know. but he's all we've got right now.

198
00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.359
<i>It's</i> Generation Game<i>.</i>

199
00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.239
<i>Nice to see you. to see you…</i>

200
00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.920
<i>Nice!</i>

201
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.319
It's not a great time.

202
00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.319
It's a different code to get out.

203
00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:27.320
Uh…

204
00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.639
Oh. he told me to leave the door open.

205
00:16:29.640 --> 00:16:31.920
It's a bit bloody late
to tell us that now.

206
00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.040
Okay. I'm on me way.

207
00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:39.999
He's comin'.

208
00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:43.800
It's… it's work.

209
00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:47.640
No. it's not. Shaun.
That's the whole bloody problem.

210
00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:56.839
- What did he sound like?
- Who?

211
00:16:56.840 --> 00:17:00.159
- The bloke on the phone.
- I don't know. Middle Eastern?

212
00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.360
- Turkish?
- Maybe.

213
00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:07.200
- I could quit. if you want.
- Don't be stupid.

214
00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.759
We should move house.

215
00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.759
- We are not going anywhere.
- I'll not have the two of you in danger.

216
00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:17.399
We've been in danger since you started.
and we'll be in danger till you finish.

217
00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:18.919
and that is not the kind of danger

218
00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:21.559
that you get rid of by moving
round the bloody corner. Guy.

219
00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:23.720
Anyway. you're not here
to talk about that.

220
00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:26.720
- Then why am I here?
- I don't know.

221
00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:28.919
This wasn't my idea.

222
00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:34.600
This is unusual. Um…

223
00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.159
Don't get me wrong.
there's not much in this job

224
00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.199
you can get away with
describing as normal.

225
00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.959
but this… this is unusual.

226
00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.839
There isn't usually a wife. you see.

227
00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:46.200
Uh. or husband.

228
00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:49.519
And that stuff
can be quite hard to manage.

229
00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:53.159
Um. people who do this stuff
tend to be unencumbered.

230
00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:56.079
If they're not and I see it in their file.
I get shot of them. so…

231
00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:59.199
you have to be very good
to get this far with that in the file.

232
00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:02.840
And he is good. he's very good.
I mean. he's a pain in the arse. but. uh…

233
00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:06.519
He's good. This is dynamite. by the way.
What's that spice I'm tasting?

234
00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:08.159
Is that… is that nutmeg?

235
00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:10.399
You know. don't you. about the phone call?

236
00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.440
My point is. it's unusual to start with.
and then there's you.

237
00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:17.480
I mean. you're in the firm. that happens.

238
00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:20.199
They're romantic places. customs lanes.

239
00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:23.999
Um. but then I looked you up.
and that did surprise me.

240
00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:28.920
So I thought we'd better meet up.
given that you're OSA compliant.

241
00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:30.759
That was a long time ago.

242
00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:32.679
Doesn't matter
if you were a babe in arms. love.

243
00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:35.639
When you've signed the
Official Secrets Act. that's you for life.

244
00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:40.080
I did six months in Investigations.
Nothing… exciting.

245
00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:46.399
And then we had our daughter.
so now I check suitcases.

246
00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.839
- Mmm.
- But I… I don't want him doing that too.

247
00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:49.840
He won't.

248
00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.679
He'll have offered to quit. no doubt.
about the call.

249
00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:55.000
but I'm sure you saw that
for the bollocks it was.

250
00:18:57.640 --> 00:18:59.559
It was a redial from a public phone.

251
00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:02.119
so they don't have your number.
let alone your address.

252
00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.839
And. so you know. I've had
someone keep an eye on this place.

253
00:19:05.840 --> 00:19:07.760
and. uh. it's all clear.

254
00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:11.359
But I'll tell you something.
There'll come a day when he needs you.

255
00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:13.639
and I can see now that you'll deliver
when that day comes.

256
00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:15.679
Is it cumin?
Is that what I'm tasting? Cumin?

257
00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:18.919
I'll do whatever's needed. He's not
quitting. and the pie's from Tesco.

258
00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.239
So why don't you two stop pissing about.

259
00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:23.760
finish your dinner.
and get back to work. yeah?

260
00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:26.480
She's top drawer.

261
00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.120
Absolute top drawer.

262
00:19:37.880 --> 00:19:40.199
It's not havin' it.
You've locked the system.

263
00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:41.839
We could call Don.

264
00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:45.159
Is that how you want this job to end
for you? Locking yourself in a building?

265
00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:47.160
It'll end a lot worse
if they find us here.

266
00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.400
- Shaun?
- Yeah?

267
00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:02.320
You need to make a call.

268
00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:08.360
So where are you from?
'Cause it's not from round 'ere.

269
00:20:09.280 --> 00:20:12.039
- Don't tell me you've not looked that up.
- I know where you were born.

270
00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:14.679
That doesn't tell me where you're from.
or what you're from.

271
00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:16.959
Sands End. Fulham.

272
00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:19.919
- Old Fulham. the way it was.
- What does that mean?

273
00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:22.159
Shared toilets and violence.

274
00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:25.079
So how'd you end up out here?

275
00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:29.760
I had a couple of brothers that died.

276
00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.440
They were just babies. I was
their big brother. and they died. and

277
00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:36.560
my mum…

278
00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:42.880
Do you know why
there's no tube station at Sands End?

279
00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:44.679
No.

280
00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:48.200
During the plague.
they buried the bodies in Sands End.

281
00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.320
There are pits of bodies under the houses.

282
00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:55.120
My old man told me that when I was young.

283
00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:58.720
I dunno what he was thinking.
but he told me that.

284
00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:04.040
We lived next to the cement factory.

285
00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:06.120
and the dust…

286
00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:09.480
Didn't matter if you closed every window.

287
00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:11.600
it found a way in.

288
00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:18.480
After my brothers died.
I don't know if Mum blamed the dust. but…

289
00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:21.680
she started…

290
00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:25.040
scrubbing.

291
00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:30.000
Every day. every night.

292
00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:33.120
I'd watch her…

293
00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:37.360
scrub our little flat.

294
00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:43.000
I'd watch her pain.

295
00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:47.240
And my old man

296
00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.280
knew

297
00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:52.280
he had to get her out.

298
00:21:54.200 --> 00:21:56.840
Away from the dust. away from

299
00:21:57.640 --> 00:21:59.920
my brothers. away from

300
00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.680
the bodies under the house.

301
00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.200
So we came out here.

302
00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:13.280
And I was wild.

303
00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:15.840
Feral.

304
00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:21.040
But over time. the wildness got

305
00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:22.760
pushed down.

306
00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:25.720
And the pain got pushed down too.

307
00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:30.200
There's always pain.

308
00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:33.880
Doing what we do.

309
00:22:35.480 --> 00:22:37.280
There's always pain behind it.

310
00:22:39.400 --> 00:22:41.680
If I let this stuff back out.

311
00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:45.319
I don't know if I can control it.

312
00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:47.920
Yeah. but you'll do it anyway.
'cause you've got no choice.

313
00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:52.440
Because you've finally found something
where you feel like you fit.

314
00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:55.240
Something you can do that no one else can.

315
00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.560
But you need to realize
that this is the rest of your life.

316
00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:04.960
The work you're doing.
the work I did. it never leaves you.

317
00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:08.480
The… the way you look at the world. the…

318
00:23:09.000 --> 00:23:11.480
the paranoia. the fear. never goes away.

319
00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:15.839
What did you do… when you did this?

320
00:23:15.840 --> 00:23:16.960
It doesn't matter what I did.

321
00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:23.200
That can't be changed. I did what I did.
and it cost me what it cost me.

322
00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:26.960
What matters is
you need to do what I couldn't.

323
00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:31.439
You need to protect your legend.
protect yourself. and protect your family.

324
00:23:31.440 --> 00:23:35.360
and if any of that makes you want out.
then tell me now. because

325
00:23:35.880 --> 00:23:37.640
this is the only time I'll ask.

326
00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:42.840
I feel like I've been waiting
my whole life for this. Don.

327
00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:45.640
I ain't stopping now.

328
00:23:48.680 --> 00:23:51.479
Get some sleep. son. Early start tomorrow.

329
00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:53.280
Not much chance of that.

330
00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:55.480
No. No…

331
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:57.400
The nights are hard.

332
00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:01.960
The days aren't easy.
but. uh… the nights are hard.

333
00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:37.319
I'll be shuttin' down
half the bloody docks.

334
00:24:37.320 --> 00:24:38.640
Just do it.

335
00:24:54.400 --> 00:24:55.560
Well done. mate.

336
00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:59.240
- Who the fuck are they?
- Put it back on.

337
00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:04.040
Oh. shit. shit!

338
00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:09.279
- It's not working. It needs to reset.
- They're gonna know somebody's been in.

339
00:25:09.280 --> 00:25:10.639
- Let me think.
- Bailey!

340
00:25:10.640 --> 00:25:11.560
Wait.

341
00:25:13.080 --> 00:25:15.080
Bailey!

342
00:25:16.160 --> 00:25:18.240
- What are you doing?
- Come on. come on.

343
00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:23.320
Turn it off!
And show me how to turn it back on.

344
00:25:35.600 --> 00:25:36.640
Did you sleep?

345
00:25:39.520 --> 00:25:40.520
Yeah.

346
00:25:44.760 --> 00:25:47.200
I lied… to Don.

347
00:25:49.520 --> 00:25:53.560
The six months in Investigations.
it <i>was</i> exciting

348
00:25:54.520 --> 00:25:56.639
and difficult to do it properly.
like you are.

349
00:25:56.640 --> 00:26:00.400
I just…
I imagine it's a whole other world.

350
00:26:03.560 --> 00:26:05.360
You're not just doing it for you.

351
00:26:12.640 --> 00:26:13.680
I know.

352
00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:20.360
He smokes. then. does he?

353
00:26:21.040 --> 00:26:22.040
He does.

354
00:26:23.520 --> 00:26:24.800
But I'm not him.

355
00:26:26.720 --> 00:26:27.840
Glad to hear it.

356
00:26:53.240 --> 00:26:54.280
What's goin' on?

357
00:26:55.320 --> 00:26:56.440
Power outage.

358
00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:00.440
Should be good now.

359
00:27:01.640 --> 00:27:03.199
Check your wiring. though. mate.

360
00:27:03.200 --> 00:27:06.200
With these old buildings.
the rats chew through the cables.

361
00:27:45.880 --> 00:27:47.880
Didn't know he had it in him.

362
00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:54.560
S'pose I best go to work then. eh?

363
00:27:59.400 --> 00:28:00.520
You all right. mate?

364
00:28:05.360 --> 00:28:06.640
Well. I'm knackered.

365
00:28:08.120 --> 00:28:09.840
Me missus isn't happy.

366
00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:13.720
I'm scared

367
00:28:14.240 --> 00:28:15.880
pretty much all the time.

368
00:28:16.880 --> 00:28:19.399
And doing this
is actually costing me money.

369
00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:20.679
what with the petrol.

370
00:28:20.680 --> 00:28:21.720
Mmm.

371
00:28:23.400 --> 00:28:24.400
And?

372
00:28:26.880 --> 00:28:29.920
And I'm lovin' every minute of it.
and I don't want it to end.

373
00:28:31.600 --> 00:28:32.960
Then don't get caught.

374
00:28:35.040 --> 00:28:35.880
Yeah.

375
00:29:07.240 --> 00:29:09.480
- What time do you call this?
- Sorry. Eddie.

376
00:29:10.720 --> 00:29:12.440
It was the fuckin' traffic. mate.

377
00:29:14.360 --> 00:29:16.480
This place is a mess. Get it sorted.

378
00:29:48.560 --> 00:29:49.600
You're late.

379
00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:54.319
- Then you wait.
- This is a lot for a test.

380
00:29:54.320 --> 00:29:56.879
There are more. We must find them.

381
00:29:56.880 --> 00:29:58.560
It's not what we agreed.

382
00:30:00.680 --> 00:30:02.840
These are Turkish apricots.

383
00:30:04.160 --> 00:30:06.200
The greatest in the world.

384
00:30:07.480 --> 00:30:09.080
They grow in Malatya.

385
00:30:09.800 --> 00:30:11.040
My homeland.

386
00:30:11.560 --> 00:30:13.080
Hakan's homeland.

387
00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:15.800
A world you do not know.

388
00:30:16.920 --> 00:30:19.279
A world where you do not belong.

389
00:30:23.720 --> 00:30:24.840
Zeki!

390
00:30:33.640 --> 00:30:34.560
Look.

391
00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:36.760
Customs.

392
00:30:39.360 --> 00:30:40.680
What is this?

393
00:30:42.000 --> 00:30:44.599
Spot checks.
But they won't be comin' here.

394
00:30:44.600 --> 00:30:45.880
They'd better not.

395
00:31:22.480 --> 00:31:24.319
- Where's your SIO?
- Pardon?

396
00:31:24.320 --> 00:31:25.400
Oh. Christ.

397
00:31:30.640 --> 00:31:31.720
Excuse me!

398
00:31:33.920 --> 00:31:35.119
- Pull 'em.
- Who are you?

399
00:31:35.120 --> 00:31:38.759
We're running an undercover operation.
You need to pull your spot checks.

400
00:31:38.760 --> 00:31:41.519
- I wasn't notified about that.
- That's why it's called undercover.

401
00:31:41.520 --> 00:31:44.279
I'm an SIO. You can't come here
and tell me what to do.

402
00:31:44.280 --> 00:31:46.120
No. but I know a man who can.

403
00:31:47.040 --> 00:31:48.839
- <i>Yes?</i>
- I'm at Felixstowe Customs.

404
00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:51.359
You need to tell them to pull the checks.
or Guy's dead.

405
00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:53.639
<i>- Put them on.</i>
- Who's this?

406
00:31:53.640 --> 00:31:56.319
This is Angus Blake. Pull your team now.

407
00:31:56.320 --> 00:31:59.400
or I'll have you checking suitcases
at Orkney Airport tomorrow.

408
00:32:08.880 --> 00:32:11.000
<i>Dukesy. return to base. mate.</i>

409
00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:19.239
- I've found it all. Zeki.
- They're going.

410
00:32:21.040 --> 00:32:23.439
- Lucky for you.
- It's got fuck all to do with luck.

411
00:32:23.440 --> 00:32:26.959
I told you. I've got this place sewn up.
Give it ten minutes before you leave.

412
00:32:26.960 --> 00:32:28.879
I'll see you back at Green Lanes
after the drop.

413
00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:30.920
- Taner will go with you.
- No. he won't.

414
00:32:31.440 --> 00:32:33.240
It is Hakan's order.

415
00:32:36.280 --> 00:32:37.320
Fine.

416
00:32:54.760 --> 00:32:55.760
Hello?

417
00:33:00.760 --> 00:33:01.600
Where are you?

418
00:33:07.840 --> 00:33:08.840
Hiya. Dad.

419
00:33:19.400 --> 00:33:21.560
Whatever you've done.
there's a way out of it.

420
00:33:23.880 --> 00:33:24.960
Sorry. Dad.

421
00:33:26.280 --> 00:33:27.919
You're comin' home. Now.

422
00:33:27.920 --> 00:33:29.519
- I can't.
- It's not a fuckin' debate.

423
00:33:29.520 --> 00:33:32.040
If Mum sees me like this.
she'll never recover.

424
00:33:32.560 --> 00:33:35.920
I've not used for two days.
and I won't be usin' again.

425
00:33:37.720 --> 00:33:39.880
I've spoke to them. Rehab.

426
00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:44.720
They said they'll take me
when I'm three days clean.

427
00:33:46.080 --> 00:33:49.519
So pick me up tomorrow. Dad.
Take me in.

428
00:33:49.520 --> 00:33:51.480
When Mum sees me. I'll be brand new.

429
00:33:52.400 --> 00:33:55.520
- I can speak to the Army about the AWOL.
- Fuck the Army!

430
00:34:00.960 --> 00:34:03.840
Just… just come and get me tomorrow. Dad.

431
00:34:04.520 --> 00:34:05.840
Please.

432
00:34:13.440 --> 00:34:15.200
I'll be here at the crack of dawn.

433
00:34:16.000 --> 00:34:18.880
- And don't be looking like this.
- Then I need to eat. Dad.

434
00:34:32.200 --> 00:34:33.200
Thanks.

435
00:34:38.160 --> 00:34:39.480
I love you. kid.

436
00:34:41.680 --> 00:34:43.120
Hey.

437
00:34:45.120 --> 00:34:46.520
I fuckin' love you.

438
00:34:50.880 --> 00:34:52.000
Love you. Dad.

439
00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:07.439
- Middle names.
<i>- Sorry?</i>

440
00:35:07.440 --> 00:35:09.279
You think they're irrelevant.
middle names.

441
00:35:09.280 --> 00:35:11.719
But they actually have a legal purpose.

442
00:35:11.720 --> 00:35:13.799
which most people wouldn't know about...

443
00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:15.039
What have you got?

444
00:35:15.040 --> 00:35:17.719
Carter is the director
of a number of companies

445
00:35:17.720 --> 00:35:21.880
but uses his middle name
and registers them in the Isle of Man.

446
00:35:22.400 --> 00:35:24.319
Turns out I can get into
the Isle of Man system

447
00:35:24.320 --> 00:35:26.679
<i>by using the Customs and Excise Act of...</i>

448
00:35:26.680 --> 00:35:28.359
You have to be a lot quicker than this.

449
00:35:28.360 --> 00:35:31.319
One of Carter's companies
owns property in Liverpool.

450
00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:35.079
which are mostly shops and pubs.
but there is something else.

451
00:35:35.080 --> 00:35:37.599
- You got an address for Carter?
<i>- I've got an address.</i>

452
00:35:37.600 --> 00:35:40.079
Whether or not he lives there
is another matter.

453
00:35:40.080 --> 00:35:41.039
<i>Go on.</i>

454
00:35:41.040 --> 00:35:45.319
5C Dawson Park Apartments.
Lord Street. Liverpool.

455
00:35:45.320 --> 00:35:46.479
Thanks. Erin.

456
00:35:46.480 --> 00:35:47.680
Good luck.

457
00:35:52.920 --> 00:35:55.119
His mate's just seen me
fixing the electricity.

458
00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:57.360
Can't exactly be hanging around the flat
the same day.

459
00:36:00.240 --> 00:36:02.319
Fine. You keep an eye on this place.

460
00:36:02.320 --> 00:36:05.200
- Covert entry is a two-person job.
- Then I won't go in.

461
00:36:15.080 --> 00:36:19.359
<i>…off to the side here
is Speedy Gillespie in trap number three.</i>

462
00:36:19.360 --> 00:36:21.360
<i>A dual-purpose performer</i>…

463
00:36:26.920 --> 00:36:29.119
A fiver. Yeah. yeah…

464
00:36:37.880 --> 00:36:39.720
Gotta spread your bets. in't ya?

465
00:36:42.000 --> 00:36:43.760
Get us a cup of tea with that?

466
00:36:44.240 --> 00:36:46.240
Yeah. a cup of tea. one sugar.

467
00:36:48.600 --> 00:36:50.920
Hang on. Yeah. yeah. it is.

468
00:36:53.040 --> 00:36:54.759
Thought you said you won on him last week.

469
00:36:54.760 --> 00:36:56.680
No. lost two ton on him.

470
00:36:57.200 --> 00:37:00.599
Our John made 50 on him last week.
as well as those at five to one.

471
00:37:00.600 --> 00:37:03.400
Yeah. Laddie's here. Let's take it easy.

472
00:37:10.520 --> 00:37:11.919
Shit.

473
00:37:13.840 --> 00:37:16.560
Armed police!
Stay where you are! Move. move!

474
00:37:17.480 --> 00:37:19.959
- Pursue the suspects!
- Armed police! Get down!

475
00:37:19.960 --> 00:37:22.040
- Out the way!
- Get down!

476
00:37:25.240 --> 00:37:26.920
Suspect's there.
Moving outside!

477
00:37:27.760 --> 00:37:28.960
Let's go.

478
00:37:37.720 --> 00:37:39.199
- Where did they go?
- This way!

479
00:37:39.200 --> 00:37:42.119
…<i>gaining on Lucky Strike
for the second time…</i>

480
00:37:45.680 --> 00:37:46.720
Dump it.

481
00:37:51.520 --> 00:37:54.080
<i>…now in the lead.
and coming right behind…</i>

482
00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:04.880
Stop!

483
00:38:15.080 --> 00:38:18.279
Your lad's out.
and we gave him the show he wanted.

484
00:38:18.280 --> 00:38:20.719
Thanks. pal. I owe you one.

485
00:38:20.720 --> 00:38:23.280
<i>We got the gear too. I tell you what. Don.</i>

486
00:38:24.360 --> 00:38:26.000
He's a bloody nutter. that one.

487
00:38:27.440 --> 00:38:28.320
Yeah.

488
00:38:29.840 --> 00:38:30.880
Yeah. he is.

489
00:40:49.960 --> 00:40:51.480
Looks like Ian Rush is off.

490
00:40:52.560 --> 00:40:54.600
Yeah. gutted.

491
00:40:55.320 --> 00:40:57.479
Do you remember his goals against Benfica?

492
00:40:57.480 --> 00:41:00.239
- Yeah. I was there.
- Get out of here! You were there?

493
00:41:00.240 --> 00:41:01.599
Yeah.

494
00:41:01.600 --> 00:41:04.600
Yeah. me old man ran a bus
from the Royal Arch pub.

495
00:41:06.240 --> 00:41:08.200
- In the Crocky?
- Yeah.

496
00:41:09.640 --> 00:41:11.160
I thought you were from Bootle.

497
00:41:13.160 --> 00:41:14.200
Well. I am.

498
00:41:14.720 --> 00:41:17.120
That's a long way
for your auld fella to go for a pint.

499
00:41:20.320 --> 00:41:21.360
Divorce.

500
00:41:25.320 --> 00:41:26.440
That's a shame.

501
00:41:30.320 --> 00:41:33.000
About Rush. He's a great player.

502
00:41:34.440 --> 00:41:36.880
Yeah. great player.

503
00:41:44.040 --> 00:41:47.639
I fuckin' told you that would 'appen.
That was amateur night. start to finish.

504
00:41:47.640 --> 00:41:48.839
Watch your mouth.

505
00:41:48.840 --> 00:41:51.639
First off. he's a liability.
Keep him away from me.

506
00:41:51.640 --> 00:41:53.839
- Who do you think you're talkin' to?
- See what I mean?

507
00:41:53.840 --> 00:41:56.000
You let him speak to me like this. Hakan?

508
00:42:02.960 --> 00:42:05.200
Zeki. enough.

509
00:42:06.040 --> 00:42:08.720
We need him more than we need you.

510
00:42:23.200 --> 00:42:24.599
What happened?

511
00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:26.000
The police were there.

512
00:42:27.560 --> 00:42:28.960
He got us out.

513
00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:32.079
- How did the police know?
- Not from me.

514
00:42:32.080 --> 00:42:34.480
I could have got 25 years
for that shit show.

515
00:42:38.440 --> 00:42:40.519
Does Liverpool know about Felixstowe?

516
00:42:40.520 --> 00:42:41.600
No.

517
00:42:42.720 --> 00:42:45.559
Well… that's somethin'.

518
00:42:45.560 --> 00:42:47.760
But next time. we do it my way.

519
00:42:48.560 --> 00:42:50.320
Or there won't be a next time.

520
00:43:20.200 --> 00:43:21.560
You shouldn't have gone in.

521
00:43:23.840 --> 00:43:26.800
We needed to know if he lives there.
Now we do.

522
00:43:28.200 --> 00:43:31.080
And I needed to understand him. Now I do.

523
00:43:40.280 --> 00:43:42.920
- Yeah.
- You have a rat in your house.

524
00:43:43.520 --> 00:43:45.040
Tell me when you've caught it.

525
00:43:47.840 --> 00:43:52.040
Carter. I've made a couple of calls.
and there's a problem.

526
00:43:52.560 --> 00:43:56.239
That new lad I've got on the van.
he's not… not who he said he was.

527
00:43:56.240 --> 00:44:01.080
He's. uh… He had papers. Carter.
like proper parole papers.

528
00:44:03.360 --> 00:44:04.799
Have you got a name?

529
00:44:07.000 --> 00:44:08.800
Fuckin' donkey.

530
00:44:15.960 --> 00:44:17.680
- Yeah?
- Look up this name.

531
00:44:18.200 --> 00:44:20.199
Call me back when you know who he is.

532
00:44:31.480 --> 00:44:33.760
<i>So. uh… so what… what do we do now?</i>

533
00:44:34.920 --> 00:44:36.040
<i>We wait.</i>

534
00:45:24.120 --> 00:45:25.920
<i>There was nothin'
anyone could've done.</i>

535
00:45:27.600 --> 00:45:29.840
He was already dead
when the paramedics got there.

536
00:45:32.960 --> 00:45:35.880
There will be a post-mortem. but

537
00:45:37.080 --> 00:45:40.160
there were signs of recent heroin usage.

538
00:45:42.240 --> 00:45:45.000
Stupid bastard.

539
00:45:45.800 --> 00:45:48.600
Stupid little bastard.

540
00:45:49.920 --> 00:45:51.520
How could he have done it?

541
00:45:54.600 --> 00:45:57.600
We can keep this out the
newspapers. We know he served his country.

542
00:45:58.120 --> 00:46:00.240
We will catch the scumbags
that are selling it.

543
00:46:00.760 --> 00:46:02.080
I can promise you that.

544
00:46:02.600 --> 00:46:06.200
They've got a start on us.
but the tide's turning.

545
00:46:07.040 --> 00:46:08.880
We're working with the communities now.

546
00:46:11.440 --> 00:46:14.080
That'll be the priest.

547
00:46:14.600 --> 00:46:17.160
Tell him we need him. Eddie.
Tell him we need him now.

548
00:46:23.080 --> 00:46:25.159
- Hello?
- Get back here now.

549
00:46:28.120 --> 00:46:29.120
I can't.

550
00:46:29.960 --> 00:46:32.999
<i>Get back here.
or I'll send someone to fetch you.</i>

551
00:46:52.240 --> 00:46:53.480
It's Eddie McKee.

552
00:47:25.080 --> 00:47:28.159
- Yeah.
- 37. five foot eight. brown hair. Scouser?

553
00:47:28.160 --> 00:47:29.399
That's him.

554
00:47:29.400 --> 00:47:32.920
<i>Yeah. he. uh… he lives in Manchester.
but it's worse than that.</i>

555
00:47:34.000 --> 00:47:35.239
What?

556
00:47:35.240 --> 00:47:39.360
He gave evidence in a VAT trial
in Preston last year

557
00:47:40.800 --> 00:47:42.880
on behalf of Her Majesty's Customs.

558
00:47:45.160 --> 00:47:48.359
<i>Listen. if… if it was serious.
he wouldn't be VAT.</i>

559
00:47:48.360 --> 00:47:50.440
he wouldn't be Manchester. he'd be London.

560
00:47:51.560 --> 00:47:54.879
And if London Customs were working
Liverpool. I'd have heard about it.

561
00:47:54.880 --> 00:47:55.800
Address?

562
00:48:00.680 --> 00:48:03.520
45 Henkel Street. Eccles.

563
00:48:04.160 --> 00:48:07.119
Carter. mate. listen.
he's a Customs officer. You cannot...

564
00:48:21.800 --> 00:48:23.639
- Piss off.
- Yeah. okay.

565
00:48:23.640 --> 00:48:25.040
I'll deal with you later.

566
00:48:38.840 --> 00:48:40.680
That kid that Jed brought in.

567
00:48:42.640 --> 00:48:43.800
he's Manchester Customs.

568
00:48:45.640 --> 00:48:47.160
<i>He can't have got anythin'.</i>

569
00:48:48.600 --> 00:48:50.640
<i>But we don't take chances.</i>

570
00:48:51.160 --> 00:48:53.800
{\an8}<i>Take the lads and see to it.</i>

571
00:48:55.920 --> 00:48:56.840
<i>How?</i>

572
00:48:59.240 --> 00:49:00.360
<i>Light him up.</i>

573
00:49:06.560 --> 00:49:07.480
<i>Life.</i>

574
00:49:08.160 --> 00:49:09.560
<i>I'd get life for that.</i>

575
00:49:11.560 --> 00:49:12.840
<i>Then don't get caught.</i>

576
00:49:20.240 --> 00:49:21.320
Fuck!

577
00:49:22.880 --> 00:49:24.880
<i>…taking charge
of this game now.</i>

578
00:49:26.040 --> 00:49:27.719
<i>Hope that brown...</i>

579
00:50:22.080 --> 00:50:23.959
- They're coming.
- What? Where?

580
00:50:23.960 --> 00:50:26.239
- Here.
- Come with us.

581
00:50:26.240 --> 00:50:27.359
- We gotta go.
- What?

582
00:50:27.360 --> 00:50:29.199
- Just trust me.
- Who are they?

583
00:50:29.200 --> 00:50:30.999
- What is it?
- It's okay. sweetheart.

584
00:50:31.000 --> 00:50:32.959
We're just going on a little adventure.

585
00:50:32.960 --> 00:50:34.999
Let's get you and your bunny
in the car. all right?

586
00:50:35.000 --> 00:50:36.719
- Mummy's coming too. darlin'.
- Who are ya?

587
00:50:36.720 --> 00:50:39.359
- What are you doin' in my house?
- Come with us. We're from Customs.

588
00:50:39.360 --> 00:50:42.319
Oh. it's you lot. then. is it.
tellin' him he can be bloody James Bond?

589
00:50:42.320 --> 00:50:43.520
Come with us. You're in danger.

590
00:50:51.040 --> 00:50:52.880
- Jump in.
- Okay.

591
00:50:53.400 --> 00:50:55.320
Let's go. let's go.

592
00:50:56.000 --> 00:50:57.400
Come on. come on. come on.

593
00:51:30.400 --> 00:51:32.759
- Chuck 'em.
- They'll hear it.

594
00:51:32.760 --> 00:51:33.960
I said chuck 'em.

595
00:51:52.360 --> 00:51:54.079
Shit. Let's go.

596
00:51:54.080 --> 00:51:56.240
Come on. let's fuckin' move!

597
00:52:32.520 --> 00:52:35.520
If we'd had 'em nicked.
they'd know we're on 'em.

598
00:52:38.880 --> 00:52:41.320
- Just fuckin' catch 'em.
- We will.

599
00:52:52.560 --> 00:52:53.840
What do we do now?

600
00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:57.520
We need another way in.

600
00:52:58.305 --> 00:53:58.814
